{"seq":1,"slug":"narrative-theory","title":"叙事理论基础","stage":"DONE","category":"storytelling-narrative","chapterCount":4,"docCount":12,"url":"/h/storytelling-narrative/narrative-theory","rating":{"composite":3.69,"verdict":"stable","groups":{"quality":3.8,"coverage":3.25,"positioning":4.5,"strategic":3.33},"weights":{"quality":0.3,"coverage":0.25,"positioning":0.2,"strategic":0.25},"profile":{"composite":3.21,"verdict":"neutral","uScore":2.5}},"introMarkdown":"# 叙事理论基础\n\n叙事是人类最古老、最基本的意义建构方式。从远古时代的篝火旁口耳相传，到今天的电影、小说、游戏与短视频，故事始终是人类理解世界、传递经验、建立共情的核心媒介。叙事理论（Narratology）试图回答一个根本问题：**什么让一个故事\"有效\"？** 它从结构、人物、技巧和形式四个维度，揭示故事之所以能打动人心的底层规律。\n\n本知识库从自学者的视角出发，系统梳理叙事领域的核心理论与实践方法。第一章聚焦**故事结构**——从亚里士多德的三幕式到坎贝尔的英雄之旅，理解故事的\"骨架\"如何搭建；第二章探讨**人物设计**——弧光、动机、冲突与对白如何赋予角色生命力；第三章深入**叙事技巧**——视角选择、展示而非告知、张力与节奏等\"手艺\"层面的问题；第四章则拓展到**类型与形式**——不同体裁的叙事惯例、短篇与微叙事的特殊规律，以及跨媒体叙事的当代实践。\n\n无论你的目标是写小说、做编剧、设计游戏剧情，还是在日常工作中讲好一个商业故事，叙事理论都能提供可迁移的思维框架。本模块的学习路径建议：先通读结构与人物两章建立整体认知，再根据个人兴趣深入技巧或类型章节。\n","chapters":[{"seq":1,"slug":"story-structure","title":"故事结构","docCount":3,"url":"/h/storytelling-narrative/narrative-theory/story-structure","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"three-act-structure","title":"三幕结构——故事的经典骨架 (Three-Act Structure)","url":"/h/storytelling-narrative/narrative-theory/story-structure/three-act-structure"},{"seq":2,"slug":"heros-journey","title":"英雄之旅——跨文化的故事原型 (The Hero's Journey)","url":"/h/storytelling-narrative/narrative-theory/story-structure/heros-journey"},{"seq":3,"slug":"story-circle-beats","title":"故事圈与节拍——当代创作者的实用工具 (Story Circle & Beat Sheets)","url":"/h/storytelling-narrative/narrative-theory/story-structure/story-circle-beats"}]},{"seq":2,"slug":"character-design","title":"人物设计","docCount":3,"url":"/h/storytelling-narrative/narrative-theory/character-design","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"character-arc","title":"人物弧光——角色的内在变化轨迹 (Character Arc)","url":"/h/storytelling-narrative/narrative-theory/character-design/character-arc"},{"seq":2,"slug":"motivation-conflict","title":"动机与冲突——故事的动力系统 (Motivation & Conflict)","url":"/h/storytelling-narrative/narrative-theory/character-design/motivation-conflict"},{"seq":3,"slug":"dialogue-voice","title":"对白与声音——让角色开口说话 (Dialogue & Voice)","url":"/h/storytelling-narrative/narrative-theory/character-design/dialogue-voice"}]},{"seq":3,"slug":"narrative-techniques","title":"叙事技巧","docCount":3,"url":"/h/storytelling-narrative/narrative-theory/narrative-techniques","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"point-of-view","title":"视角与叙述声音——谁在讲这个故事 (Point of View & Narrative Voice)","url":"/h/storytelling-narrative/narrative-theory/narrative-techniques/point-of-view"},{"seq":2,"slug":"show-dont-tell","title":"展示而非告知——叙事写作的核心美学 (Show, Don't Tell)","url":"/h/storytelling-narrative/narrative-theory/narrative-techniques/show-dont-tell"},{"seq":3,"slug":"tension-pacing","title":"张力与节奏——让读者\"放不下书\"的秘密 (Tension & Pacing)","url":"/h/storytelling-narrative/narrative-theory/narrative-techniques/tension-pacing"}]},{"seq":4,"slug":"genre-form","title":"类型与形式","docCount":3,"url":"/h/storytelling-narrative/narrative-theory/genre-form","docs":[{"seq":1,"slug":"genre-conventions","title":"类型叙事与惯例——创作者与受众的契约 (Genre Conventions)","url":"/h/storytelling-narrative/narrative-theory/genre-form/genre-conventions"},{"seq":2,"slug":"short-form-narrative","title":"短篇叙事与微叙事——在极限篇幅内讲好故事 (Short-Form & Micro Narrative)","url":"/h/storytelling-narrative/narrative-theory/genre-form/short-form-narrative"},{"seq":3,"slug":"transmedia-storytelling","title":"跨媒体叙事——一个故事世界，多种讲述方式 (Transmedia Storytelling)","url":"/h/storytelling-narrative/narrative-theory/genre-form/transmedia-storytelling"}]}]}